      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Parameters",
      "contextAfter": "`value`: The value to replace in `theSet`. If this value does not already exist in `theSet`, the function does nothing. You may pass the value itself instead of a pointer if it is pointer-size or less. The equal callback provided when `theSet` was created is used to compare. If the equal callback was `NULL`, pointer equality (in C, ==) is used. If `value`, or any other value in `theSet`, is not understood by the equal callback, the behavior is undefined.",
